You are Cursor AI working inside the EDU Platform monorepo.

HARD RULES (do not violate):

- Source of truth must be read before coding:

  1. docs/ai/PROJECT_RULES.md
  2. docs/rubric.md
  3. docs/architecture/decisions.md
  4. docs/architecture/domains.md
  5. docs/architecture/data-model.md
  6. docs/architecture/event-catalog.md
  7. docs/api/\* (e.g., docs/api/auth.md)
  8. docs/security/\* (if present)

- If any requirement is missing/unclear: DO NOT INVENT.
  Propose the missing spec update inside docs first, then implement.

- All IDs are UUID (no incremental IDs).

- Services do NOT share databases and must not do cross-service joins.

- Platform Architecture is mandatory:

  - Microservices
  - Event-Driven Architecture using Kafka (primary event bus)

- CQRS policy (important clarification):

  - CQRS is mandatory as a PRINCIPLE (separate Commands from Queries in code structure) for all services.
  - Strong CQRS (separate read model/projections) is NOT mandatory for every service.
    It must be implemented clearly in at least 1–2 services to satisfy rubric, and documented in docs/architecture/decisions.md.

- Inside each service use Layered/Hexagonal structure:

  - presentation/ (controllers, DTOs, swagger decorators)
  - application/ (use cases, commands/queries, ports)
  - domain/ (entities, invariants, domain errors)
  - infrastructure/ (prisma repos, kafka producer/consumer, redis)
  - shared/ (cross-cutting utilities)

- Security:

  - JWT access + refresh with refresh rotation.
  - Never store raw refresh tokens or raw password reset tokens; store hashes only.
  - RBAC is mandatory: TEACHER/STUDENT/ADMIN (permissions optional).
  - No hardcoded credentials/users in code (only controlled dev seed if required).
  - CORS must be explicit and environment-based.
  - Rate limiting is required (at least per IP/per route in auth; Redis-backed).

- Events (Kafka):
  - Follow docs/architecture/event-catalog.md
  - No sensitive data in events (no passwords/tokens/secrets)
  - Include correlationId and actorUserId when available
  - Topic naming: <domain>.<aggregate>.<event>
  - Prefer Outbox pattern; if not implemented, document why in service README and decisions.md.
  - Consumers must be idempotent (at-least-once delivery).

QUALITY BAR:

- Each service must expose Swagger/OpenAPI with real DTOs, examples, auth decorators, and error responses.
- Each service must have baseline unit + integration/e2e tests (minimal but real).
- Services must be Dockerized (Dockerfile per service). Local dev uses docker compose. Prod uses Terraform.

OUTPUT / EDITING:

- Prefer editing/creating files using Cursor Apply actions.
- Only use FILE MANIFEST output when the user explicitly asks for copy/paste or when not able to apply changes.
- No placeholders. No pseudo-code. No TODO-only files. All code must compile.
- Keep code consistent: TypeScript, NestJS, Prisma for Postgres persistence (unless the service spec explicitly chooses a different DB type).

DEFAULTS:

- Language for code comments/docstrings: English.
- Commit messages: Conventional Commits.
